The best approach for `File.*` and `Directory.*` is the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's battle-tested and provides a complete `IFileSystem` interface. No need to write custom wrappers.

## Recommendation: Adopt `System.IO.Abstractions`

### 1. Install the package

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

### 2. Register in DI (`Program.cs`)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

Your `ReportGenerator` would become:

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {DateTime.UtcNow:O}\nMachine: {Environment.MachineName}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        Console.WriteLine($"Report written to {reportPath}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```bash
dotnet add <YourTestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("Sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
Assert.Contains("Report: Sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
```

### Bonus: Your class also has other statics

I noticed `ReportGenerator` also uses `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.*`. Quick guidance:

| Static | Recommended Abstraction |
|---|---|
| `DateTime.UtcNow` | **`TimeProvider`** (built-in on .NET 10) — register `TimeProvider.System`, inject `TimeProvider`, call `timeProvider.GetUtcNow()`. Test with `FakeTimeProvider` from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`. |
| `Environment.*` | Custom **`IEnvironmentProvider`** — wrap only `GetEnvironmentVariable` and `MachineName` (what you actually use). |
| `Console.*` | Custom **`IConsole`** with a `WriteLine(string)` method. |

Want me to generate wrappers for those too, or migrate the call sites in `ReportGenerator` to use `IFileSystem`?
